Release the global_control storage before unloading the libraries:
global_control_release() frees it with cache_aligned_deallocate(),
which calls scalable_aligned_free() from libtbbmalloc when it is
loaded, so it must run before dynamic_unlink_all(). The order became
wrong with https://github.com/uxlfoundation/oneTBB/pull/1346, which added
global_control_release() after dynamic_unlink_all().

Reported upstream in https://github.com/uxlfoundation/oneTBB/pull/1849#issuecomment-6978073786
--- src/tbb/governor.cpp.orig
+++ src/tbb/governor.cpp
@@ -119,8 +119,8 @@
 #endif /* TBB_USE_ASSERT */
 
     system_topology::destroy();
-    dynamic_unlink_all();
     global_control_release();
+    dynamic_unlink_all();
 }
 
 rml::tbb_server* governor::create_rml_server ( rml::tbb_client& client ) {
